[{"id":"VRCE-5-51-1","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":51,"verse":1,"english":"Hearing those words of his, the high-souled ten-necked one spoke to his brother a speech consonant to season and place,","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.726,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-53-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5051001","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6f30dd2a4465c8da91a6153105ef1828a032fe073a9f55a5f2f96d7f3df94989","compact":"c1f6354a72d575bebc326dd8d417dd4f42f6a8a81148a61b4d36a0325a82f87e","nasal":"c1f6354a72d575bebc326dd8d417dd4f42f6a8a81148a61b4d36a0325a82f87e"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-51-2","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":51,"verse":2,"english":"Properly had you spoken, to slay a messenger is improper. But let him be punished with any chastisement save slaying.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.867,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-53-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5051002","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8d18ac7a2c51dca2432e8c6b8a3637765b3a459e2fa82d42d0b5ad24901bc405","compact":"1fddab185a0a8367418c7243b4c30b501e13e79168a4eb8152ca74ad7afa38e2","nasal":"1fddab185a0a8367418c7243b4c30b501e13e79168a4eb8152ca74ad7afa38e2"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-51-3","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":51,"verse":3,"english":"Certainly the tail is a darling ornament to a monkey. Therefore let his tail be set on fire anon; and this having been consumed, let him go away.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.814,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-53-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5051003","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2fcbf9446321183b834db1aee604e46001c5af6b26e63794410946566ca37277","compact":"c9f12baccd9105a6a63a9208fe986ea8e0fc76c5ec351e04b061880da82a41d5","nasal":"48970cf79ad1aab2f444712d7ab79f10a55262c8ea6d153ab5a1463b6d61d476"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-51-4","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":51,"verse":4,"english":"Then shall his best friends and kindred and acquaintances see him crest-fallen, with his person deformed.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.676,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-53-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5051004","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e9f49f5b2ffb51b77af09bc96ff95e93b0f8bc17a60311654c0537e792e2b63d","compact":"0cfca8f98ce53951bbd9e38a8ad49e9e799e4d0ffec90afec742a089db77e678","nasal":"146a9914f6ed3f0a997243951053acb83624dab71fd44e6efe4adcffa8453bb7"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-51-5","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":51,"verse":5,"english":"The lord of Rākşasas ordered, With his tail in flames, let this one be taken all round Lankā containing terraces.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.768,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-53-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5051005","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ccecc874b09eaebfb9f33110076474e5aa71c612c26e6bd2a9c0a7a20bac00d6","compact":"ba397c4671d94339048bb7b53ed6381c63da5eb94cbc376f9f63a4c811805d5c","nasal":"038b6f9b610b73d6b18301ab195c94cde3e1addb1592b26f575a152d7a0f442d"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-51-6","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":51,"verse":6,"english":"Hearing his words, the Raksasas, cruel through wrath, cover up his (Hanumān's) tail with worn pieces of cotton cloth.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.904,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-53-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5051006","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cf1bc06836eee65664a8fad5b092f0d1a0ebccf927d5b9591a77b103acdc7621","compact":"821b2a1b3cf5bf6b0f30b013614e4907a6a49923280c4a41836f3e473d662f82","nasal":"8f561632d79e718ab47c1329543c7d3166ebb9eb44dd52d3029ba593ed32a12a"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-51-7","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":51,"verse":7,"english":"Thereat, even as fire in a forest increase on getting dry fuel, the mighty monkey grew in dimensions on his tail being wrapped up.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.855,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-53-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5051007","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"90f7f27575d212ed5f5654284ff331b83ea17ec398c03d7e20bcd0a276ce16df","compact":"ac3d90235dffd14100611c194fcb699b56a7bdf0d15b5c43d09cf37e988b761c","nasal":"a4a4227c519f855933600f2008b40e08ed98cc25af2295035b44dd03ce749281"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-51-8","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":51,"verse":8,"english":"Having soaked (the cloth) in oil, they set fire to it. Thereat with his soul overpowered with rage and hatred, and his countenance like the risen sun, he lashed them with his flaming tail.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.704,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-53-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5051008","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f1e301739154fe39f59ec5f2134aead04128f4293951ac94f696e5130029d98a","compact":"4f41676c29c8a767085c8ca890b6874b4fcd370b0e6e97bc871948d297778448","nasal":"4f41676c29c8a767085c8ca890b6874b4fcd370b0e6e97bc871948d297778448"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-51-9","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":51,"verse":9,"english":"Having soaked (the cloth) in oil, they set fire to it. Thereat with his soul overpowered with rage and hatred, and his countenance like the risen sun, he lashed them with his flaming tail.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.742,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-53-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5051009","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"54a1abcc77f8d0e4985c194c2c947006a4dd506f0656e00166a551ccfc2d7e55","compact":"de93abee892d726085da874bb687d7dbd54e96ac72537f35429716670ed31793","nasal":"369f123a515daaebbbc21ed6878ee98bb7d2ee9596e839d1bd72e9130147b347"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-51-10","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":51,"verse":10,"english":"That hero (being bound), entertained a purpose in harmony with the season. \"Albeit bound, the Rākşasas cannot forsooth cope with me. Snapping these bonds, I shall, darting up, again slaughter these.\"","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.468,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-53-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5051010","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c14bb75fff02c04bea2b4986832913d6f5df11d6cd4ac88578e674ab4293540e","compact":"b89d3e6da97acf1c49ddaa54a6d64928afd9642482e7b4d3049cfc0f10047c27","nasal":"b89d3e6da97acf1c49ddaa54a6d64928afd9642482e7b4d3049cfc0f10047c27"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-51-11","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":51,"verse":11,"english":"That hero (being bound), entertained a purpose in harmony with the season. \"Albeit bound, the Rākşasas cannot forsooth cope with me. Snapping these bonds, I shall, darting up, again slaughter these.\"","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.894,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-53-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5051011","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"79d559234729a8a82bc7baf8b7094c9e9508c63d9e08f3810cd1b0bd8e0d23fa","compact":"6c7c8ff64346ff42f3a9994fe199ca5920e6e96a06ef2a7c9229d50d6b1f6c29","nasal":"6c7c8ff64346ff42f3a9994fe199ca5920e6e96a06ef2a7c9229d50d6b1f6c29"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-51-12","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":51,"verse":12,"english":"I can slay all these Rākşasas in battle; but I suffer this (maltreatment) for not marring the (pure delight) Rāma shall derive from my deed.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-53-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5051012","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ec4f5a344f65cc80765c928dc21925c9935178dd5ea9fe9763a402e076e2f197","compact":"b67db199e2b3bb912907d08c776a526264a3b55ba307c57b321df3ada0df90ac","nasal":"b67db199e2b3bb912907d08c776a526264a3b55ba307c57b321df3ada0df90ac"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-51-13","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":51,"verse":13,"english":"I shall once more range around Lankā. Let this be so. At night I could not satisfactorily examine the fortifications.* (Another meaning is:-lts places inaccessible on account of works.) For certain, by me is to be beheld Lankā when night has departed. Let them bind me anew. The Rākşasas pain me by setting fire to my tail; but my mind dose not tire.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.554,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-53-13","DUTT-5-53-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5051013","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"01d0f06832327a75dca1fcb7075fa0839d8d778d7cefafac0f503e708144948b","compact":"e18e7733009724a0d296bf57def1f45970339c01b4d647df1d246f48232e4b2d","nasal":"c9f58f13c6b675911540ec9c4bd81290683482d4c891175e7a826939d19a06ec"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-51-14","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":51,"verse":14,"english":"For certain, by me is to be beheld Lankā when night has departed. Let them bind me anew. The Rākşasas pain me by setting fire to my tail; but my mind dose not tire.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.701,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-53-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5051014","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"319d8febfb2a0a8127e62acab26b5853a24b97356c24829bb3361db6b0bf671c","compact":"227468c3e1fe09f451c87cf460fed9fdca59816bfde1c717f69a5c1764c3983f","nasal":"3c0a9df7453242849949dadb6f7606bc2615785571845ddc8c03956ba1ac09eb"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-51-15","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":51,"verse":15,"english":"Then the Raksasas, rejoicing greatly, went off, taking that mighty monkey endowed with strength, an elephant (in prowess) among monkeys. And blowing conchs and trumpets, and bruiting it abroad by various actions, (Publishing Hanuman's penalty) those Raksasas of cruel deeds took (Hanumān) about the city (of Lankā).","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.879,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-53-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5051015","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7f48b4a7c62b00115dafcccbaed60fd2143a99748bc8009f355b5fcd04f738f0","compact":"2864c46b02a951f772f68ce4e5a384202a2f33d703935f277d6cdd62f5cf22f1","nasal":"c478a3ddf1cc3ed682e301446b8c2896cac71fbc9c9b74ea1f2813305db49c8a"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-51-16","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":51,"verse":16,"english":"Then the Raksasas, rejoicing greatly, went off, taking that mighty monkey endowed with strength, an elephant (in prowess) among monkeys. And blowing conchs and trumpets, and bruiting it abroad by various actions, (Publishing Hanuman's penalty) those Raksasas of cruel deeds took (Hanumān) about the city (of Lankā). And led by those Rākşasas, that subduer of enemies, Hanumān, experienced delight, and going about the mighty metropolis of the Rākşasas, the redoubted monkey surveyed variegated cars, enclosed court-yards, wellordered terraces, streets thronged with edifices, crossings, by-ways, and the interiors dwellings.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.472,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-53-15","DUTT-5-53-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5051016","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e385e594011f82448785ddad47c7d1ccbc1a3493a708b1c39417d9ccf234bf8f","compact":"edf97cb9ef65b016d9e03b0cc0b0a52a20722949e1e5127bc64a36c266f7d9bb","nasal":"81a98c612a30ebdd17e9044c70c07ca1969ba826e267648b6efe9055982de4b0"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-51-17","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":51,"verse":17,"english":"And led by those Rākşasas, that subduer of enemies, Hanumān, experienced delight, and going about the mighty metropolis of the Rākşasas, the redoubted monkey surveyed variegated cars, enclosed court-yards, wellordered terraces, streets thronged with edifices, crossings, by-ways, and the interiors dwellings.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.823,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-53-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5051017","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"34efb249373b2cb3587e1694cffb83014ce4d5988ffa9bcbf8c7998a852cd0e8","compact":"912eb604c9edee2dbd53180fb310e561b5d791936563deda224005ff4f0d0003","nasal":"912eb604c9edee2dbd53180fb310e561b5d791936563deda224005ff4f0d0003"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-51-18","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":51,"verse":18,"english":"And led by those Rākşasas, that subduer of enemies, Hanumān, experienced delight, and going about the mighty metropolis of the Rākşasas, the redoubted monkey surveyed variegated cars, enclosed court-yards, wellordered terraces, streets thronged with edifices, crossings, by-ways, and the interiors dwellings.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-53-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5051018","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"45ad0b628faf167b21c073f137f987cfdb3e8